.TH CANTCP-CLI 1 "2026-09-28" "cantcp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cantcp-cli \- command-line client for cantcp servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cantcp-cli
.I command
[\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cantcp-cli
connects to cantcp servers (SocketCAN over TCP). It listens to CAN frames,
sends frames and reads the server statistics.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B listen
Connect and print the received frames in the candump log format or as JSON
lines.
.TP
.B send
Send one frame built from
.B \-\-id
and
.BR \-\-data ,
or every frame read from a candump-style file or stdin.
.TP
.B stats
Fetch the server statistics over HTTP and print a table or the raw JSON.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.TP
.B help
Print the top-level help.
.SH COMMON FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIpath\fR
JSON configuration file. Default:
.IR /etc/cantcp/cantcp-cli.json .
.TP
.B \-\-server \fIhost:port\fR
cantcp server address (default
.IR 127.0.0.1:29536 ).
.TP
.B \-\-stats-server \fIURL\fR
Server statistics URL (default
.IR http://127.0.0.1:29537 ).
.TP
.B \-\-tls
Connect over TLS 1.3.
.TP
.B \-\-tls-ca \fIfile\fR
CA file used to verify the server certificate; without it the system roots
are used.
.TP
.B \-\-tls-cert \fIfile\fR, \fB\-\-tls-key \fIfile\fR
Client certificate and key for mutual TLS.
.TP
.B \-\-tls-server-name \fIname\fR
Server name to verify instead of the host from
.BR \-\-server .
.TP
.B \-\-tls-insecure
Skip certificate verification. Debugging only: the connection can be
intercepted.
.TP
.B \-\-log-level \fIlevel\fR, \fB\-\-log-format \fIformat\fR
Log level and format.
.SH LISTEN FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-id \fIhex\fR, \fB\-\-mask \fIhex\fR
Identifier filter: a frame passes when
.IR "frame.id & mask == id & mask" .
A zero mask accepts every frame.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON object per frame.
.TP
.B \-\-count \fIn\fR, \fB\-\-timeout \fId\fR
Stop after n frames or after the given time.
.TP
.B \-\-can-name \fIname\fR
Interface name used in the candump output (default
.IR can0 ).
.SH SEND FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-id \fIhex\fR, \fB\-\-data \fIhex\fR
Frame identifier and payload. An identifier above 0x7FF is extended; use
.B \-\-ext
to force the extended form.
.TP
.B \-\-fd
Send a CAN FD frame;
.B \-\-brs
sets the bit rate switch flag.
.TP
.B \-\-count \fIn\fR, \fB\-\-interval \fId\fR
Send the frame n times with the given delay.
.TP
.B \-\-input \fIfile\fR
Read candump-style lines; "-" reads stdin. A positional file argument works
the same way.
.SH FRAME SYNTAX
The candump-style input accepts:
.PP
.nf
123#11223344            classic frame
12345678#1122           extended identifier
123#R                   remote frame
123##1DEADBEEF          CAN FD, flag digit: bit 0 BRS, bit 1 ESI
(1696000000.1) can0 123#1122   candump log line
.fi
.PP
Empty lines and lines starting with "#" are skipped.
.SH CROSS-COMPILATION
The binaries are pure Go. Build them on any platform for any Go target:
.PP
.nf
CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./cmd/cantcp-cli
CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm64 go build ./cmd/cantcp-cli
CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm GOARM=7 go build ./cmd/cantcp-cli
.fi
.PP
The published release packages use linux/amd64, linux/arm64 and linux/armv7.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cantcpd (8),
.I https://github.com/burn-lab-dev/cantcp
